  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Vocabulario escolar y universitario**",
      "",
      "| Palabra | Significado | Nota |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| *school · primary · secondary* | colegio, primaria, secundaria | |",
      "| *university · college* | universidad / centro | *college* en EE. UU. = universidad |",
      "| *degree · bachelor's · master's · PhD* | grado, máster, doctorado | |",
      "| *subject · course · module* | asignatura · curso · módulo | |",
      "| *mark (UK) · grade (US)* | nota | *I got a good mark.* |",
      "| *pass · fail · retake* | aprobar · suspender · repetir | |",
      "| *attend · assist* | asistir a / ayudar | ✘ *assist a class* |",
      "",
      "**Verbos de estudio:** *study (estudiar en general), learn (aprender), revise (repasar), cram (empollar de última hora), take notes, do research, hand in an essay, sit an exam (presentarse a un examen), graduate in / from.*",
      "",
      "**Colocaciones**",
      "",
      "- *do / study a degree in Law* · *get a degree · graduate from university.*",
      "- *take / sit an exam* (presentarse) vs *pass an exam* (aprobar).",
      "- *write an essay · give a presentation · do homework · hand in coursework.*",
      "- *get good / bad marks · repeat a year · drop out.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo — falsos amigos**",
      "",
      "- *Lecture* ≠ 'lectura' (es 'clase magistral'); 'lectura' = *reading*.",
      "- *Career* ≠ 'carrera universitaria' (esa es *degree*); *career* = trayectoria profesional.",
      "- *Exam* es examen; *exercise* no es 'examen'.",
      "- *Student* es cualquiera que estudia; *pupil* es un niño en colegio (UK).",
      "- *College* en UK = centro de formación post-16 años.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *scholarship* /ˈskɒləʃɪp/ · *degree* /dɪˈɡriː/ · *graduate* (verbo) /ˈɡrædʒueɪt/, (sustantivo) /ˈɡrædʒuət/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I assisted the class.",
        "right": "I attended the class.",
        "note": "Attend = asistir."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I study a career in Law.",
        "right": "I'm doing a degree in Law.",
        "note": "Career ≠ carrera."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": [
